WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.520
Some celebrities have earned a serious reputation
for difficulty among their co-stars so much

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.100
so that other actors don't ever want to work
with them again. From simple personality conflicts

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.090
to deranged name-calling and everything in
between, let's take a look at some of the

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.800
most infamous co-star beefs and how they got
started.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.280
Jim Carrey and Tommy Lee Jones

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.710
When Jim Carrey starred as the Riddler in
Batman Forever, he was at the height of his

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.179
comedic career. But his co-star Tommy Lee
Jones who played Harvey Dent was definitely

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:33.160
not a fan of Carrey's slapstick style. Director
Joel Schumacher confirmed that Jones had something

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.790
of an attitude on set, telling Entertainment
Weekly:

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.120
"Jim Carrey was a gentleman, and Tommy Lee
was threatened by him. I'm tired of defending

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.900
overpaid, over-privileged actors."

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.920
The night before filming a scene together,
Carrey and Jones ran into each other at a

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.990
restaurant. When Carrey approached Jones'
table to say hello, he didn't get quite the

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.020
greeting he expected. Carrey told Howard Stern
that:

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.120
"He got up, kind of shaking, and hugged me
and said, 'I hate you. I really don't like

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.200
you.' And I was like, 'Wow. What's going on
man?' And he said, 'I cannot sanction your

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:01.780
buffoonery.'"

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.360
“Very few people are both a summer and a
winter, but you pull it off nicely.”

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.360
Wesley Snipes and Ryan Reynolds

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.920
Reading Patton Oswalt's account of his time
on the set of 2004's Blade Trinity is arguably

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.140
far more interesting than watching the movie
itself. According to Oswalt, director David

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.840
S. Goyer shouldn't be blamed for the way the
movie turned out, as he spent half of his

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:29.920
time dealing with the erratic behavior of
leading man Wesley Snipes.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:36.380
“And he'd walk by his trailer and this wall
of pot stench would just just woah and just

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.280
push you to the side”

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.189
He also claimed Snipes tried to strangle the
director at one point, which led to Goyer

00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:45.600
hiring a bunch of bikers as bodyguards. According
to Oswalt:

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.480
"That freaked Wesley out so much that, for
the rest of the production, he would only

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.909
communicate with the director through Post-It
notes. And he would sign each Post-It note

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:54.760
'From Blade.'"

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:59.619
It wasn't just Goyer that Snipes clashed with,
however. The mercurial action star also failed

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:04.649
to get along with co-star Ryan Reynolds, apparently
refusing to even call him by his name. Reynolds

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:08.149
laughed when he was asked if he would ever
consider reuniting with Snipes for a fourth

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:10.780
Blade movie, answering with an emphatic "no."

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.140
Will Smith and Janet Hubert

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.700
If you're a dedicated Fresh Prince of Bel-Air
fan, you're probably aware that the actress

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.760
who played Aunt Vivian was replaced halfway
through the series but you might not know

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.920
why. Janet Hubert portrayed Aunt Viv on the
show until 1993, when she was replaced with

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.780
Daphne Reid, who continued in the role until
Fresh Prince ended its run in 1996.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.920
According to accounts from show insiders and
even Hubert herself, Smith and his other co-stars

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.599
were needlessly cruel to her on the set. For
his part, Smith knocked down Hubert's allegations

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:46.709
in a 1993 interview with an Atlanta radio
station, claiming she had a bad attitude while

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:47.799
filming and adding:

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:50.460
"No matter what, to her I'm just the Antichrist."

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.380
In 2011, Hubert fired back, telling TMZ that
she'd never work with Smith again.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.040
Tom Sizemore and Val Kilmer

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.780
Throughout the '90s, Tom Sizemore's star was
on a meteoric rise in Hollywood, thanks in

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:07.269
particular to his roles in great dramatic
films like 1995's Heat, which he featured

00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:11.769
in alongside Val Kilmer. But when Kilmer and
Sizemore reunited five years later on the

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:16.370
set of Red Planet, things weren't so rosy.
Reportedly, Kilmer was upset when he learned

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.769
that the production had paid to ship Sizemore's
exercise equipment to Australia, where filming

00:03:20.769 --> 00:03:21.700
was taking place.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:26.520
According to Sizemore's memoir By Some Miracle
I Made It Out of There, a shouting match erupted

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:31.680
which ended with Tom throwing a 50-pound weight
at Kilmer. Later, a producer asked Sizemore

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.060
to avoid hitting Kilmer in the face when they
got into their next fight. Tom complied, dutifully

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.510
slugging Kilmer in the chest and telling him:

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.820
"I'm never going to another planet with you
again."

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:45.300
Time heals all wounds, however, and the two
former co-stars had finally buried the hatchet

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.860
as of 2014.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.460
Robert Downey Jr. and Terrence Howard

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:54.329
Terrence Howard has never been shy about discussing
his falling out with Iron Man co-star Robert

00:03:54.329 --> 00:04:00.220
Downey Jr. In 2013, Howard appeared on Bravo's
Watch What Happens Live, discussing the three-picture

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.560
deal which the studio had originally offered
him.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:09.020
“They came to me with the contract and said
look, we will pay you ⅛ of what we contractually

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.800
had for you.”

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.900
He went on to put the blame firmly on Downey's
shoulders.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:18.120
“And I called my friend, and I'd helped
him get the first job, and he didn't call

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.519
me back for three months."

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:23.340
It would take another three years for the
pair to finally patch up their differences,

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:27.080
when they reunited at the 2016 wedding of
director Brian Grazer.

